WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:07.589
Speaker 1: I am so glad to have the opportunity
today to, I guess, bring you more evidence

00:00:07.589 --> 00:00:11.530
that my instinct yesterday, when we looked
at clips of Donald Trump's former attorney

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:15.540
general William Barr, saying Trump's election
lies were B.S. and whatever.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.600
It doesn't make Barr a good guy.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.349
It doesn't even make him a sensible guy.

00:00:20.349 --> 00:00:27.140
And the day after these clips went viral of
William Barr saying Trump brought in a clown

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:30.869
show of lawyers after the election, all of
this stuff.

00:00:30.869 --> 00:00:36.370
When pressed, William Barr still says I'd
vote for Trump over a Democrat if he ran in

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:37.789
2024.

00:00:37.789 --> 00:00:40.719
This is exactly what I was talking about yesterday.

00:00:40.719 --> 00:00:45.260
Bill Barr after saying Trump lied about the
election.

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:50.219
He incited the attack on January 6th, et cetera,
et cetera.

00:00:50.219 --> 00:00:54.610
He told Savannah Guthrie yesterday, Well,
if it's Trump versus a Democrat, of course

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:57.579
I'm going to vote for Trump because Democrats
are really, really bad.

00:00:57.579 --> 00:01:01.200
This is why I say these are not good people.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.289
These people are not our friends or any of
it.

00:01:03.289 --> 00:01:05.119
Bill Barr wants to sell books.

00:01:05.119 --> 00:01:06.119
That's all that's going on.

00:01:06.119 --> 00:01:07.119
Take a listen.

00:01:07.119 --> 00:01:10.450
Speaker 2: You say in your book, it's time
for the party to move on from Trump.

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:15.760
Liz Cheney has said he is not fit to serve
and should not be ever near the Oval Office

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:16.760
again.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:17.760
Speaker 3: Do you agree with that?

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:22.149
Well, I certainly have made it clear I don't
think he should be our nominee, and I'm going

00:01:22.149 --> 00:01:24.540
to, you know, support somebody else for the
nominee.

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:29.869
But if he is the nominee and you have your
choice, is Donald Trump or whoever is running

00:01:29.869 --> 00:01:33.430
on the Democratic side, would you vote for
him?

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:37.390
Because I believe that the greatest threat
to the country is the progressive agenda being

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:39.340
pushed by the Democratic Party.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:41.790
It's inconceivable to me that I wouldn't vote
for the Republican.

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:47.090
A nominee so favorite, if he lied about the
election and threatened democracy, as you

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:48.160
write in your book.

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:49.920
Well, it's better than a Democrat.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.500
It's hard to project what the facts are going
to turn out to be three years hence.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:57.730
But as of now, it's hard for me to concede
that I wouldn't vote for the report,

00:01:57.730 --> 00:02:02.050
Speaker 1: even though he's a threat to democracy.

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:08.039
A threat to our country incited a riot, lied
about who won the election.

00:02:08.039 --> 00:02:09.590
Brought out a clown show of lawyers.

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:14.690
I mean, listen, progressives are really the
threat.

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:17.000
This is why these people are so dangerous,
guys.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:23.569
And this is why I told you he stumbled across
some small factoid, some small element of

00:02:23.569 --> 00:02:24.569
truth.

00:02:24.569 --> 00:02:26.790
But this is not a this is not a good guy.

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:28.260
And it's the same thing with Liz Cheney.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:33.840
At the end of the day, Liz Cheney maybe wouldn't
vote for Trump against a Democratic nominee,

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:38.319
but she still did vote with Trump, something
like 88 percent of the time when Trump was

00:02:38.319 --> 00:02:39.319
president.

00:02:39.319 --> 00:02:41.960
Just as a reminder, here's what William Barr
said about Trump yesterday.

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:45.099
But remember, he'd still vote for Trump over
a Democrat,

00:02:45.099 --> 00:02:52.720
Speaker 3: and I told him that all this stuff
was bull and about election fraud.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:59.870
And you know, it's wrong to be shoveling it
out the way his team was, and he started asking

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:03.780
me about different theories and I had the
answers.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:08.400
I was able to tell them, This is wrong because
of this, you're trying to set him straight.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:09.519
Yes.

00:03:09.519 --> 00:03:10.940
And you know, he listened.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:14.099
He he he was obviously getting very angry
about this.

00:03:14.099 --> 00:03:19.879
I said, OK, well, look, I understand you're
upset with me and I'm perfectly happy to tender

00:03:19.879 --> 00:03:22.150
my resignation.

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:24.680
And then, Oh, you slept to the desk and he
slapped the desk and he said, accepted.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:29.100
Accept it and then boom, he slapped it again.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.549
Accept it.

00:03:30.549 --> 00:03:31.549
Go home.

00:03:31.549 --> 00:03:32.549
Don't go back to your office.

00:03:32.549 --> 00:03:33.549
Go home.

00:03:33.549 --> 00:03:38.159
Speaker 1: So William Barr saying that William
Barr also referring to all those wacky lawyers

00:03:38.159 --> 00:03:41.380
that Trump hired to try to flip the election
as a clown show

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:45.920
Speaker 3: and about election fraud.

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:51.849
And you know, it was wrong to be shoveling
it out the way his team was.

00:03:51.849 --> 00:03:54.430
And then he also
Speaker 4: told Trump what he thought of his

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:56.200
legal team.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:57.200
Not a lot.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:00.810
Speaker 3: I said the reason you are where
you are is because you wheeled out a clown

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:03.330
show of lawyers, a clown show.

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:05.380
Yeah, clown car or something like that.

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:06.380
I said, Yeah.

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:10.720
Speaker 1: So anyway, he'd still vote for
Trump if there's a Democrat.

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:13.750
I mean, he says, this guy is not fit to serve.

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:14.989
He's a threat to the country.

00:04:14.989 --> 00:04:16.160
Terrible for democracy.

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:17.160
All this stuff.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:21.610
Well, but now I mean, listen, I'm not going
to vote for Joe Biden completely, you know,

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:27.060
innocuous milquetoast Democrat who, you know,
will be lucky to have major accomplishments

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:31.350
that that change American society or the economy
in any serious way.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:35.920
It's actually almost worse that, you know,
there's the people who think Trump's great

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:39.640
like, OK, well, I disagree with you.

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:42.630
And I would I would have that argument with
you.

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:47.100
But these people realize Trump is not a threat
to democracy.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:48.510
Unfit to serve.

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:53.000
And they still say, Well, if it's Joe Biden
or Carmel, I mean, I just can't imagine I

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.460
would ever vote for a Democrat.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:58.040
It's completely and totally bonkers.

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:02.110
And this is exactly what I was talking about
when I was saying, this guy wants to sell

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:03.110
a book.

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:04.570
